WEBVTT

00:01.290 --> 00:03.430
Okay, next.

00:03.970 --> 00:06.750
I'm Yamada Kento! I wanna be a ladies' man.

00:06.750 --> 00:10.410
But I'll be faithful once
I have a girlfriend, so hit me up!

00:11.740 --> 00:13.930
Okay, thank you.

00:13.930 --> 00:15.870
Next up is, let's see...

00:16.250 --> 00:17.400
Iwakura-san.

00:21.420 --> 00:22.280
To battle!

01:54.420 --> 01:55.900
Self-intros?

01:55.900 --> 01:58.550
Yeah. Nothing serious, I'm guessing.

01:58.550 --> 02:00.680
I'll just keep things casual.

02:00.680 --> 02:02.560
That explains the lack of sleep.

02:03.680 --> 02:06.110
Smile, okay? Just smile!

02:06.110 --> 02:09.940
Don't worry! Nobody's gonna
ask you to tell a joke!

02:09.940 --> 02:11.440
Shmiwe?

02:11.750 --> 02:12.860
Like this?

02:18.490 --> 02:19.340
Is that a dude?

02:19.340 --> 02:20.220
No way!

02:20.220 --> 02:21.800
But hey, look...

02:26.730 --> 02:28.380
Is this better?

02:30.880 --> 02:33.950
Gosh, I can't even tell the difference!

02:33.950 --> 02:35.800
But you're cute either way!

02:35.800 --> 02:36.960
You think?

02:38.170 --> 02:40.290
Thanks for the advice, Nao-chan.

02:42.090 --> 02:44.890
I'm Iwakura Mitsumi.
My birthday is March 3rd.

02:44.890 --> 02:47.780
I came here from Ikajima,
Ishikawa Prefecture!

02:47.780 --> 02:49.270
Check out those bags...

02:49.630 --> 02:51.100
It's around here, by the way.

02:51.100 --> 02:52.650
- Whoa!
- That's so far!

02:52.650 --> 02:54.260
You moved here all alone?

02:54.260 --> 02:56.420
No, I'm staying with a relative.

02:56.420 --> 02:57.190
Huh...

02:57.840 --> 03:00.760
I want to be a government official,
which is why I applied to a Tokyo school.

03:00.760 --> 03:01.960
Whoa!

03:01.960 --> 03:02.550
Thanks for...

03:02.550 --> 03:03.700
Why the government?

03:03.700 --> 03:04.680
Why...?

03:05.210 --> 03:06.580
It's a bit of a long story.

03:06.580 --> 03:10.570
Don't worry! Nobody's gonna
ask you to tell a joke!

03:11.960 --> 03:14.200
Nao-chan, I...

03:15.800 --> 03:18.660
I'm a woman who goes above and beyond!

03:19.790 --> 03:22.720
Because I was born to lead, obviously!

03:31.580 --> 03:32.560
Next up!

03:33.170 --> 03:37.320
I'm Shima Sousuke, born and raised in Tokyo.

03:37.320 --> 03:39.650
I enjoy physical activities.

03:39.650 --> 03:41.200
My dream is, well...

03:41.200 --> 03:42.740
I don't have one just yet.

03:42.740 --> 03:45.660
Oh, wait. I wouldn't mind
working for Iwakura-san.

03:50.240 --> 03:51.410
Shima-kun!

03:52.610 --> 03:55.100
He really is a great guy!

03:55.790 --> 03:59.180
His given name is "Sousuke," huh?

03:59.180 --> 04:01.800
Written with "satoi,"
the kanji for "clever"... Sato...

04:03.600 --> 04:04.720
Satonosuke?!

04:07.880 --> 04:10.000
You're kidding! What a coincidence!

04:10.000 --> 04:13.660
His fur's even the same color! Amazing!

04:14.990 --> 04:16.180
Oh, come on...

04:18.260 --> 04:19.450
Next on our agenda...

04:19.450 --> 04:23.980
We need class officers, one boy and one girl.

04:23.980 --> 04:25.110
Any volunteers?

04:25.900 --> 04:27.450
Okay, Iwakura-san.

04:27.450 --> 04:29.460
Nobody else?

04:29.460 --> 04:32.450
Then Iwakura-san will be
class officer for the girls.

04:36.740 --> 04:38.590
Then we know who the boy'll be, too!

04:39.970 --> 04:41.510
Shima for the boys!

04:42.380 --> 04:44.130
Count me in!

04:49.030 --> 04:50.170
Let's do this.

04:50.170 --> 04:51.270
Yeah.

04:51.270 --> 04:53.470
We should write this on the board, right?

04:53.470 --> 04:54.390
I'll do it.

04:54.790 --> 04:55.810
Huh?

04:55.810 --> 04:57.220
Hang on...

04:57.220 --> 04:59.320
There's no way, right?

05:00.200 --> 05:04.070
Are those two, like, hitting it off?

05:04.410 --> 05:08.290
Is Shima-kun just a natural player?
Or is it all calculated?

05:08.870 --> 05:10.840
Maybe I should dig into this a bit.

05:11.900 --> 05:12.940
Karaoke?

05:12.940 --> 05:13.720
Yep!

05:13.720 --> 05:17.210
We finished our post-entrance tests,
so I was thinking we could go.

05:17.210 --> 05:18.410
Sounds good! I'm in!

05:18.410 --> 05:19.680
I wanna blow off some steam!

05:19.680 --> 05:21.820
What are the cheap places around here?

05:21.820 --> 05:24.240
Karaoke... I've never been before.

05:24.240 --> 05:27.140
Hey, guys! You wanna join us after school?

05:27.140 --> 05:29.010
Oh, are we invited too?

05:29.010 --> 05:31.850
You too, Shima-kun.
Iwakura-san will be there.

05:31.850 --> 05:34.600
Really? Guess I'll go, then.

05:36.850 --> 05:39.610
Are all of you coming?

05:40.600 --> 05:42.860
I can go today.

05:43.230 --> 05:46.570
Yay, I can't wait! I haven't
gone to karaoke in forever!

05:47.760 --> 05:49.750
Murashige Yuzuki...

05:49.750 --> 05:53.580
I kinda didn't wanna invite
a beauty queen like her.

05:54.590 --> 05:55.750
Iwakura-san.

05:58.870 --> 06:02.130
You shouldn't take everything
Shima-kun says at face value.

06:03.320 --> 06:05.720
Y'know... how do I say it?

06:05.720 --> 06:10.970
When a guy's that hot, he's bound to
have lots of girls fall for him, right?

06:10.970 --> 06:12.180
Uh... right.

06:12.670 --> 06:17.430
If he lets it get to him,
it causes issues with people.

06:17.430 --> 06:20.710
So guys like him tend to be
nice to everyone as a rule.

06:21.940 --> 06:24.830
Oh, sorry to spring this
on you out of nowhere.

06:24.830 --> 06:27.440
I just don't wanna see you
get hurt, you know?

06:27.440 --> 06:28.330
Oh.

06:29.110 --> 06:30.950
Right, gotcha.

06:33.870 --> 06:37.670
Yeah, that makes sense.
I'd let it go to my head a little.

06:39.050 --> 06:40.550
But, like...

06:41.720 --> 06:44.140
I wish she hadn't said it.

06:46.010 --> 06:47.460
How long will you be staying?

06:47.460 --> 06:48.590
Two hours.

06:49.090 --> 06:51.020
Please use the drink bar over there.

06:51.020 --> 06:52.090
Thank you.

06:54.100 --> 06:57.060
Two hours, so that's...

06:57.060 --> 06:58.780
Huh? Iwakura-san?

06:58.780 --> 07:00.060
We pay after we're done.

07:00.060 --> 07:02.350
Is this your first time at karaoke?

07:02.350 --> 07:03.870
There weren't any near me!

07:04.930 --> 07:07.820
Some places do ask you to pay up front.

07:08.110 --> 07:11.980
I... I see.

07:11.980 --> 07:14.210
Don't take it at face value.

07:14.210 --> 07:16.560
Shima-kun's nice to everyone.

07:19.560 --> 07:21.750
You'll be there.

07:24.000 --> 07:25.540
He's gonna join the light music club.

07:25.540 --> 07:26.250
Oh?

07:28.350 --> 07:29.480
Queued up a song yet?

07:33.090 --> 07:34.710
Are you a good singer?

07:34.710 --> 07:36.010
Nope.

07:36.510 --> 07:37.670
Was that your dialect just now?

07:37.670 --> 07:38.520
Huh? I guess.

07:38.520 --> 07:41.520
My tambourine's on fire today!

07:42.480 --> 07:45.150
Yeah. Karaoke's...

07:46.230 --> 07:48.530
super loud!

07:54.340 --> 07:55.280
Hey, there.

07:56.610 --> 07:59.620
Murashige-san is so pretty.

08:00.240 --> 08:02.090
Doesn't this bother you?

08:03.330 --> 08:07.000
She's clearly using you
to get closer to Shima.

08:07.000 --> 08:10.130
And she's mocking your dialect,
even when it's easy to understand.

08:10.580 --> 08:11.930
You've picked up on it, right?

08:12.750 --> 08:13.880
I...

08:14.280 --> 08:16.410
I didn't have a clue!

08:18.990 --> 08:20.730
Let me know if you want to leave.

08:20.730 --> 08:22.490
I wouldn't mind bouncing either.

08:34.700 --> 08:36.270
This is hard.

08:37.640 --> 08:40.640
There were only eight people
in my middle-school class,

08:40.640 --> 08:44.710
so I never thought building
relationships would be so difficult.

08:45.710 --> 08:48.090
You can never tell what people are thinking.

08:56.470 --> 08:57.470
Fumi...

08:58.170 --> 09:01.060
Mitsumi-chan, how are ya doing?

09:01.450 --> 09:03.190
Can't have changed in a day, huh?

09:04.230 --> 09:05.840
Are ya home yet?

09:07.900 --> 09:10.030
Nah, right now...

09:10.900 --> 09:12.190
I'm at karaoke!

09:12.190 --> 09:14.310
What? Karaoke?!

09:14.310 --> 09:17.300
I've only been once, back when
I was knee-high to a grasshopper.

09:17.300 --> 09:19.360
Well, this is my first time.

09:19.360 --> 09:21.940
I'm here with a bunch of people from class.

09:21.940 --> 09:23.930
Lucky you! Having fun?

09:23.930 --> 09:24.770
Yeah.

09:24.770 --> 09:27.140
I'm having a blast.

09:27.500 --> 09:29.120
That's a lie, ain't it?

09:29.750 --> 09:30.810
No, it's...

09:30.810 --> 09:32.470
Yeah, you're lying.

09:32.470 --> 09:34.590
You're kinda wishing you
could go home, aren't ya?

09:35.470 --> 09:36.970
Fumi... Are you a psychic?

09:38.180 --> 09:41.350
I just know how you sound
when you're feeling down.

09:41.350 --> 09:44.850
You even called at the perfect time, too.

09:44.850 --> 09:48.100
Really? Maybe it was telepathy.

09:50.150 --> 09:55.000
If I said, "I wish you were here with me,"
that'd make her worry, wouldn't it?

09:55.950 --> 09:56.930
Fumi?

09:56.930 --> 09:58.060
Yeah?

09:58.060 --> 10:02.590
Uh, how did we become friends, again?

10:02.590 --> 10:05.700
Beats me. I don't remember.

10:05.700 --> 10:06.760
Figures.

10:07.290 --> 10:11.280
Oh, but I remember not liking you
much back in kindergarten.

10:11.710 --> 10:13.670
Wh-Wh-Why?!

10:13.670 --> 10:17.340
You were always pouting.
I thought you were scary.

10:17.340 --> 10:19.500
But you're actually real sweet.

10:20.630 --> 10:23.810
I just didn't know it back then.

10:23.810 --> 10:26.220
Eek!

10:26.630 --> 10:31.000
And now we call each other
every day. Who'da thunk it?

10:32.220 --> 10:33.640
Thanks, Fumi.

10:34.270 --> 10:35.510
S'all good.

10:35.990 --> 10:38.490
I'll call you back later.

10:38.490 --> 10:39.910
To vent.

10:39.910 --> 10:41.790
I'll be waiting.

10:48.710 --> 10:51.000
Oh, welcome back, Iwakura-san.

10:51.000 --> 10:51.930
Thanks.

10:51.930 --> 10:53.750
I've been wondering...

10:53.750 --> 10:56.000
Is that pin, like, a fashion statement?

10:56.000 --> 10:57.460
What does that mean?

10:59.320 --> 11:02.760
Wait, how am I supposed to tell?
I've known her two days.

11:03.200 --> 11:05.920
There's been no point
overthinking this stuff.

11:05.920 --> 11:07.530
Yeah, it's an accessory!

11:08.760 --> 11:10.860
Oh, who's next?

11:12.020 --> 11:13.720
Whoa!

11:13.720 --> 11:14.760
Nice, let's go!

11:14.760 --> 11:16.270
Go for it, Iwakura-san!

11:17.460 --> 11:20.530
And Shima-kun, I'm sorry
for trying to overanalyze you!

11:28.950 --> 11:32.960
Du-du-du-dun, march on now!

11:32.960 --> 11:35.960
Tokojiro!

11:35.960 --> 11:39.480
Where are you hauling that carrot off to?

11:39.480 --> 11:42.970
Hop, step, and jump, you haul it off.

11:42.970 --> 11:46.350
Du-du-du-dun, come on now!

11:46.860 --> 11:49.980
Tokojiro!

11:49.980 --> 11:53.310
Where are you hauling that carrot off to?

11:53.310 --> 11:57.750
When your ears droop, see you tomorrow!

12:01.190 --> 12:03.360
Iwakura-san, you're so fun!

12:03.360 --> 12:05.200
I loved Tokojiro as a kid!

12:05.670 --> 12:08.200
I'm gonna pick a nostalgic song too!

12:09.150 --> 12:12.240
I just didn't know it back then.

12:14.110 --> 12:15.200
Someday...

12:16.300 --> 12:21.210
Will I ever be able to laugh and reminisce
like that with anyone here, too?

12:22.810 --> 12:24.830
That would be so nice.

12:28.090 --> 12:30.500
Man, I could murder a beef bowl right now.

12:30.500 --> 12:31.480
Yeah, same.

12:31.480 --> 12:33.480
All that singing made me hungry.

12:33.480 --> 12:34.400
Hey.

12:35.340 --> 12:36.730
Give me your chat ID.

12:36.730 --> 12:38.940
S-Sure.

12:38.940 --> 12:41.050
Er... Where is it?

12:41.050 --> 12:43.780
See the "Add a friend" button
at the top of your friends list?

12:44.540 --> 12:48.070
You know, I only came to play nice,
since this was the first time and all.

12:48.070 --> 12:50.040
I don't really like karaoke, to be honest.

12:50.680 --> 12:54.150
But thanks to you, Mitsumi, I had fun today.

12:59.290 --> 13:00.940
Well, I got somewhere to be, so bye.

13:00.940 --> 13:03.220
Huh? You're leaving, Murashige-san?

13:03.220 --> 13:04.540
Bye-bye!

13:05.350 --> 13:07.940
You can never tell what people are thinking.

13:08.800 --> 13:12.560
So I'll try to understand them,
little by little.

13:12.560 --> 13:14.820
I guess we're calling it, then?

13:14.820 --> 13:15.620
Sounds good.

13:15.620 --> 13:16.040
Later!

13:16.040 --> 13:17.190
Shoot!
Later!

13:18.470 --> 13:20.920
Shima-kun, do you watch movies and stuff?

13:20.920 --> 13:21.940
Sometimes, yeah.

13:21.940 --> 13:24.960
Oh, sweet! With your girlfriend?

13:24.960 --> 13:27.450
Hmm... It's not that.

13:28.360 --> 13:32.450
Egashira-san, maybe you
should loosen up a little?

13:32.900 --> 13:35.030
You'll have more fun that way.

13:35.030 --> 13:37.710
Huh? Why would you say that?

13:41.020 --> 13:42.460
Why would you say<i> that?</i>

13:43.960 --> 13:45.720
Hey! Iwakura-san!

13:46.560 --> 13:50.170
We live in the same direction, right?
Let's head home together.

13:50.170 --> 13:52.720
He really does resemble Satonosuke.

13:52.720 --> 13:54.010
Sato-chan, do you...

13:54.990 --> 13:56.610
Huh? "Sato-chan"?

13:56.610 --> 13:58.470
I-I'm so sorry!

13:58.470 --> 14:00.270
Who are you mixing me up with?

14:01.070 --> 14:02.480
My family...

14:02.920 --> 14:03.760
dog.

14:05.770 --> 14:06.410
Your dog?!

14:06.410 --> 14:08.610
It's just... You've got the
same color fur and stuff!

14:08.920 --> 14:10.690
Oh, you mean my hair?

14:10.690 --> 14:12.500
Well, it <i>is</i> kinda wavy and soft.

14:12.500 --> 14:13.580
Wanna touch it?

14:21.060 --> 14:23.050
Wow, look at you go.

14:29.300 --> 14:32.150
Hey. Can I call you Mitsumi-chan?

14:32.150 --> 14:33.050
Sure.

14:38.510 --> 14:40.730
Morning, Iwakura-san!

14:40.730 --> 14:42.560
Good morning, Kinomoto-san.

14:42.560 --> 14:44.400
Ta-da!

14:44.400 --> 14:47.180
I found this cute little thing
on the way home from karaoke,

14:47.180 --> 14:49.350
so I tried following your example.

14:49.350 --> 14:51.240
How do you like the star?

14:51.590 --> 14:53.450
Cute. Very cute.

14:53.450 --> 14:55.740
Yay, thanks.

14:55.740 --> 14:58.670
You got a buncha recruitment flyers, huh?

14:58.670 --> 15:03.500
Yeah. They all remembered me from my speech.

15:03.500 --> 15:06.580
Why don't we take over the world
of high-school quizzing together?

15:06.580 --> 15:10.010
Let's discuss the future of our environment!

15:10.010 --> 15:13.100
I keep getting invited to the brainy clubs.

15:13.100 --> 15:14.970
Good for you.

15:14.970 --> 15:17.000
Have you picked your club, Kinomoto-san?

15:17.000 --> 15:17.770
Yep.

15:17.770 --> 15:19.900
I'll be joining the dance club!

15:21.020 --> 15:22.480
Cute!

15:22.480 --> 15:24.570
Morning, Kinomoto-san.

15:24.570 --> 15:25.730
You too, Mitsumi-chan.

15:25.730 --> 15:26.990
"Mitsumi-chan"?

15:26.990 --> 15:27.940
Good morning.

15:27.940 --> 15:30.140
When did you get on first-name basis?

15:30.140 --> 15:31.070
Lucky me, huh?

15:31.070 --> 15:33.930
You can call me Sato-chan, too.

15:33.930 --> 15:35.620
Look, that's my dog's name, okay?

15:35.620 --> 15:37.810
Oh my god! What's going on?!

15:37.810 --> 15:39.800
Oh, morning, Egashira-san.

15:39.800 --> 15:41.120
Morning.

15:41.620 --> 15:42.870
Clubs?

15:42.870 --> 15:45.590
I think I'm gonna pass.
I've got cram school.

15:46.220 --> 15:48.750
Yeah, you start to wonder
if you can juggle both.

15:48.750 --> 15:50.430
I'm joining the English conversation club.

15:50.430 --> 15:52.010
It'll help with exams,

15:52.010 --> 15:54.560
and I'm sure it'll be useful in the future.

15:58.520 --> 15:59.560
And then...

16:00.750 --> 16:02.160
I nearly forgot.

16:02.160 --> 16:06.510
This is an elite prep school,
and I have a dream...

16:08.200 --> 16:11.030
And yet I started having
these silly fantasies!

16:11.030 --> 16:12.880
You okay there, Mitsumi?

16:12.880 --> 16:14.660
Yeah, I...

16:17.270 --> 16:19.580
Is this Iwakura Mitsumi-san's class?

16:23.750 --> 16:25.040
Can I help you with something?

16:25.040 --> 16:26.540
Oh!

16:26.910 --> 16:30.290
So you're the top first-year!

16:30.290 --> 16:33.380
I knew it! Your eyes shine
like nobody else's!

16:33.380 --> 16:36.360
I'm Kanechika, a second-year
and the next drama club president.

16:36.360 --> 16:39.010
Iwakura-san, are you interested in acting?

16:41.140 --> 16:42.560
U-Uh...

16:42.560 --> 16:44.270
I'm Iwakura.

16:55.160 --> 16:56.570
How cultured!

16:58.450 --> 17:00.990
Now that you mention it, it all makes sense.

17:00.990 --> 17:03.250
I couldn't spot you hidden away like that.

17:03.250 --> 17:05.350
On day one, you became "The Puker."

17:05.350 --> 17:08.840
On day two, your funny self-intro
made you "The Secret Boss."

17:08.840 --> 17:13.090
It's amazing that you got two
monikers in such a short time!

17:13.090 --> 17:16.590
Here. They're today's props, but I'll let you
have more, since you're so intriguing!

17:16.590 --> 17:20.020
Thanks... The "Secret Boss" stuff
is news to me, though.

17:20.020 --> 17:23.160
It takes talent to make
such an impression on people.

17:23.590 --> 17:25.820
What do you say? Theater is...

17:26.300 --> 17:30.590
Senpai, could you stop scaring your juniors?

17:32.090 --> 17:35.030
Oh, did I scare you?
Sorry, I got a little amped.

17:35.030 --> 17:38.160
Anyway, come see our performance today!

17:38.160 --> 17:41.880
You'll be able to boast that you
saw a star playwright at work!

17:41.880 --> 17:43.910
I'm talking about myself, of course.

17:45.960 --> 17:49.370
Hmm, he looks like he belongs on stage...

17:49.370 --> 17:50.170
Huh?

17:50.170 --> 17:52.630
Do I know you from somewhere?

17:54.140 --> 17:55.880
No, I don't think you do.

17:56.420 --> 17:57.380
Oh, okay.

17:57.380 --> 17:59.750
See you later!

18:00.920 --> 18:02.810
That guy was like a hurricane, huh?

18:02.810 --> 18:04.660
Yeah... Talk about intense.

18:05.650 --> 18:07.380
It's a sin to be so gifted!

18:07.380 --> 18:09.190
She took him seriously!

18:22.180 --> 18:25.540
Everyone's given it serious thought.

18:30.180 --> 18:31.840
I'd better pull myself together.

18:32.840 --> 18:34.180
Everyone gather up!

18:34.180 --> 18:35.180
Right!

18:39.680 --> 18:42.970
Yikes, not many first-years, huh?

18:42.970 --> 18:44.350
Yeah. Not looking good.

18:44.350 --> 18:45.260
Right?

18:46.280 --> 18:48.950
They don't have enough people
for the female parts,

18:48.950 --> 18:51.620
so Kanechika's been running around in heels.

18:51.620 --> 18:53.450
Yeah, I saw that.

18:53.450 --> 18:55.020
Oh, so that's why.

19:05.340 --> 19:07.870
You're the one who left that night!

19:07.870 --> 19:10.190
You asked for it.

19:10.190 --> 19:13.850
You said solitude was the only way
to keep a safe distance from others.

19:13.850 --> 19:15.590
That's a wild assumption.

19:16.730 --> 19:19.660
It was a conversational play
involving four characters.

19:20.330 --> 19:23.830
Most of it flew over my head, honestly.

19:23.830 --> 19:26.850
But I felt like the most exciting
discoveries and achievements

19:26.850 --> 19:32.270
are usually a product of the kind of single-
minded dedication I saw on that stage.

19:44.530 --> 19:45.780
Shima-kun.

19:46.460 --> 19:47.960
You came to watch?

19:47.960 --> 19:49.910
Yeah, kinda.

19:49.910 --> 19:51.610
Wasn't expecting you to.

19:51.610 --> 19:52.770
Really?

19:55.290 --> 19:58.570
Is it just me, or is he
not as talkative as usual?

19:59.300 --> 20:03.190
What do you do when you're having
a hard time making up your mind?

20:03.190 --> 20:04.540
Is this about clubs?

20:04.540 --> 20:06.800
Is it bothering you that much?

20:10.220 --> 20:11.560
Hmm...

20:12.260 --> 20:17.570
I tell myself that the things I'm undecided on
were never that important anyway.

20:18.210 --> 20:22.440
There are only so many important things
you can't compromise on, right?

20:23.710 --> 20:25.570
It's just the entrance ceremony.

20:26.720 --> 20:31.330
Shima-kun is light-hearted, always smiling,

20:31.770 --> 20:33.080
and kind...

20:34.370 --> 20:37.840
Anyway, Mitsumi-chan,
I kinda need to hurry today.

20:38.390 --> 20:39.620
See you tomorrow.

20:40.310 --> 20:44.600
But sometimes, he seems a little sad.

20:47.250 --> 20:49.490
A total mystery.

20:52.990 --> 20:54.320
Wanna grab something on the way home?

20:54.320 --> 20:54.730
I'm down for some fried chicken.

20:54.730 --> 20:56.310
Oh, there you are!
I'm down for some fried chicken.

20:56.310 --> 20:59.690
Hey, I remember you now!

21:00.110 --> 21:02.190
You're Kanade-kun, right?

21:03.620 --> 21:05.450
Are you confusing me with someone else?

21:05.450 --> 21:07.380
Nah, I'm talking about...

21:07.380 --> 21:09.050
Sorry, go on without me.

21:09.050 --> 21:09.870
Okay.

21:09.870 --> 21:11.730
Listen, I know I'm right!

21:11.730 --> 21:14.300
My father loved that TV show!

21:14.300 --> 21:16.230
He recorded all of it!

21:16.230 --> 21:18.500
I only watched it in middle school—

21:18.500 --> 21:20.590
Kanematsu-senpai, was it?

21:21.490 --> 21:24.590
Don't you understand?
I don't want to talk about it.

21:25.110 --> 21:29.570
It's amazing you call yourself a playwright
when you can't even pick up on that.

21:30.320 --> 21:31.620
Goodbye.

21:36.600 --> 21:38.930
Ohh?

21:41.880 --> 21:43.480
Nao-chan, you know what?

21:43.480 --> 21:45.990
I've decided not to join any clubs.

21:45.990 --> 21:47.840
Oh, is that so?

21:47.840 --> 21:49.370
But instead,

21:49.370 --> 21:51.990
I'm going to join the student council!

21:51.990 --> 21:55.120
It'll help me get some
valuable leadership experience!

21:55.120 --> 21:58.380
Ah, youth! Ah, high schoolers!

21:58.380 --> 22:00.380
Always with the big, starry-eyed dreams!

22:00.380 --> 22:01.310
Really?

22:01.310 --> 22:03.850
I'm going to stay like this
all the way to retirement.

22:03.850 --> 22:05.800
Oh, this rolly thingie feels great.

22:06.410 --> 22:07.560
Doesn't it?
